=== REASONING ===

Why the design preserves ADR-015, P1-P10 + the non-AI baseline:

ADR-015 §I1 default-off: Registry entry sets DefaultOn=false. The
SPA's gate (withAiFeature HOC) reads useSettings()'s ai_mode +
ai_features map — both must be on for the section to render.

ADR-015 §I3 baseline intact: The deterministic
GET /api/v1/analytics/lifetime handler is unchanged in JSON shape
(response key names + ordering preserved exactly). The slice
EXTRACTED ComputeLifetimeStats from the handler body so the AI
tool can call the same code path WITHOUT duplicating SQL —
critical for ADR-015 §I3 (a future change to the deterministic
envelope must propagate to both the dashboard and the AI surface
automatically). The achievement-persistence + SSE celebration side
effects are kept ONLY on the canonical handler path (the AI tool
returns achievements with UnlockedAt=nil so the read-only AI tool
NEVER triggers a celebration event or DB write).

ADR-015 §I4 zero egress: aiGuard wraps the new route with
guard.Wrap("lifetime-stats-qa"). The guard is exercised by the
Go-side TestLifetimeStatsQAAIOffHidesQuestionBox: ai_mode='off'
+ toggle on still returns 404. The SPA's gate is exercised by the
React-side TestLifetimeStatsQAAIOffHidesQuestionBox: the wrapper
component renders an empty container in off mode, even with the
toggle on.

ADR-015 §I5 hidden UI: The AILifetimeStatsQA component is
withAiFeature-wrapped so it returns null in off mode — there is
no skeleton, no banner, no greyed-out section.

ADR-015 §I6 404 routes: The Go off-mode test asserts the AI
route returns 404 with no leaked feature metadata
(lifetime-stats-qa, feature, strategy, provider, agent strings
all absent from the 404 body), and that the canonical baseline
GET /api/v1/analytics/lifetime route remains reachable.

ADR-015 §I7 per-feature: The toggle is per-feature; the off-mode
React test exercises BOTH halves of the gate (mode='off' + toggle
on, AND mode='cloud' + toggle off) to defeat the "hidden because
flag is off" trivial pass.

ADR-015 §I9 redaction: PolicyChatbot is the deny-by-default
policy (Allow=nil; every PII class redacted to a round-trip tag
including vehicle name). Because Q&A is conversational the slice
prompt was explicit: "Allowed classes: none; answers are grounded
in aggregate tools and round-trip tags". No new policy was
needed; the existing PolicyChatbot is reused verbatim, asserted
by TestStrategy_RedactionPolicyChatbot in strategy_test.go
(len(want.Allow) == 0 + Mode == ModeRedactedTags).

ADR-015 §I10 type system: The AI surface lives entirely under
/api/v1/ai/*; no field on the existing baseline JSON shape is
added or modified. The tool envelope's fields live in the AI-only
typed envelope (tools.LifetimeStatsEnvelope) returned by
query_lifetime_stats — distinct from the api.LifetimeStatsResult
that backs the canonical handler (though they currently share
field names by design for ergonomic reasons).

P1-P10 alignment:
 P1 (provider port):     handler resolves provider via
                         h.registry.For(ctx, FeatureID); never
                         imports a concrete adapter.
 P2 (settings/keys):     no key handling in slice scope; uses
                         existing aiSettingsRepo from boot.
 P3 (audit log):         no extra audit work; the dispatcher's
                         decorator chain already audits every
                         provider call.
 P4 (strategy/dispatch): Strategy implements the canonical
                         interface (FeatureID, SystemPrompt,
                         Tools, RedactionPolicy, EvalGoldens).
                         Dispatcher loop bounded by
                         aiLifetimeStatsQAMaxIterations=8.
 P5 (decorator chain):   the registered provider is already
                         wrapped in the locked decorator order
                         (redact → rate limit → cost cap → audit
                         → trace) — slice does NOT bypass.
 P6 (guards):            backend route uses guard.Wrap; SPA
                         component uses withAiFeature HOC.
 P7 (eval harness):      goldens.yaml + canned/*.yaml shipped;
                         go run ./cmd/ai-eval --feature
                         lifetime-stats-qa returns 3/3 PASS.
 P8 (eval goldens):      typical_lifetime_question +
                         zero_data_vehicle + refusal_other_vehicle.
 P9 (registry):          full RouteSet metadata populated;
                         empty arrays explicit (JobNames=[],
                         PushKinds=[]).
 P10 (baseline coexistence): LifetimeStatsPage + canonical
                         handler unchanged; AI section is mounted
                         AS A SIBLING above the hero card, not as
                         a replacement.
 P11 (Wired-or-absent): SPA component ships fully wired to the
                         backend route via useAiStream — no
                         "coming soon" placeholder.
 P12 (No placeholder buttons): the Ask button's disabled prop is
                         a computed expression (`!canAsk`), not a
                         literal `disabled`/`disabled={true}`.
                         On-mode wiring test asserts dynamic
                         disabled flips correctly when the user
                         types a question.

